msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30053"
msgid "Server-side (Dispatcharr plugin)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30054"
msgid "Recording padding: start early (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30055"
msgid "Mirrors Dispatcharr's own global recording padding setting (Settings -> DVR in Dispatcharr's web UI) -- there is no per-timer equivalent, Dispatcharr only has one global value shared by every EPG-based recording (series rules and one-time recordings matched to a guide entry), so changing this here changes it for all of them at once, the same as changing it in Dispatcharr's own UI would. Does NOT affect recurring (day-of-week) timers -- confirmed against Dispatcharr's own source that its recurring-rule scheduler never applies this setting at all, a gap on Dispatcharr's side this addon can't work around. Kept in sync with Dispatcharr's real current value on every Kodi restart, so this display doesn't go stale if it's changed another way (Dispatcharr's own UI, a different Kodi install sharing the account). Reading that current value needs no special permission, but pushing a change you make here back to Dispatcharr needs a real Dispatcharr admin account -- with a lesser account this fails silently: the value stays showing as changed here, but Dispatcharr's own setting doesn't actually move, with nothing surfaced beyond an error line in kodi.log."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30056"
msgid "Recording padding: stop late (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30057"
msgid "The end-of-recording counterpart to the start-padding setting above -- see its help text for the full explanation (global-only, EPG-based recordings only, kept in sync with Dispatcharr's real value on restart)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30058"
msgid "Dispatcharr's configured timezone (for reference)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30059"
msgid "Read-only: Dispatcharr's own configured system timezone, as its raw IANA zone name (e.g. \"America/Chicago\") -- kept in sync on every restart. When this is one of the zones the timezone dropdown below recognizes, that dropdown is auto-selected to match it, so this field mostly exists for the case where it isn't -- a concrete reference for what zone you're converting from when you have to fall back to manual offset entry, instead of having to separately check Dispatcharr's own admin panel."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30060"
msgid "Recurring timer: timezone"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30061"
msgid "Only affects recurring (day-of-week) timers -- see the manual-offset setting below for the full explanation of why this exists at all. Pick the zone that matches Dispatcharr's own configured system timezone (shown just above) and this addon computes the correct current UTC offset for it automatically, including flipping for daylight saving on its own -- no more manually updating a number twice a year. Auto-selected to match Dispatcharr's own zone on every restart when it's one of the zones listed here, so you shouldn't normally need to touch this yourself. If your zone isn't in this list, leave this on \"Manual (enter offset below)\" and use the plain numeric offset setting instead -- this addon only knows real DST transition rules for a limited set of common zones (US/Canada, UK/EU), not a full worldwide timezone database."
msgstr ""

