msgctxt "#30088"
msgid "Extra padding for sports (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30089"
msgid "Added on top of the normal end-of-recording padding above, but only for a one-time recording created directly from an EPG entry whose category Dispatcharr's guide data tags as sports, and only when its end time hasn't already been manually adjusted in Kodi's own timer-edit dialog. Sports broadcasts commonly run long (extra innings, overtime, rain delays) in a way scripted programming doesn't -- 0 disables this. Recurring and series rules aren't affected: Dispatcharr computes those recordings' own start/end times server-side, with no per-occurrence EPG entry for this addon to check against."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30047"
msgid "Improve catch-up seek reliability (experimental)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30048"
msgid "Routes catch-up/archive playback (play from guide) through the separate inputstream.ffmpegdirect addon (Kodi's official repository) instead of Kodi's own built-in seeking, which can be imprecise for raw MPEG-TS over HTTP. Experimental -- requires inputstream.ffmpegdirect to be installed, or catch-up playback will fail outright with this on. Results have been inconsistent in testing: one round found precise seeks, just slow (tens of seconds to a few minutes to land) on a several-hour recording; a later side-by-side comparison against the default, same content, found this setting 2-3x slower on every seek with no clear precision advantage over just leaving it off. Worth trying against your own content, but don't assume it's an upgrade -- leave off to use Kodi's default catch-up playback if unsure."
msgstr ""

